---
import LegalPageLayout from '../components/legal/LegalPageLayout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/sanity/data';
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="DATA PROTECTION & PRIVACY"
  subheading="UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018 compliance framework governing how Techsteps UK Limited collects, protects, and handles personal and corporate client data."
  metaTitle="Privacy Policy | UK GDPR Data Protection | Techsteps UK"
  metaDescription="Techsteps UK Privacy Policy. Comprehensive data protection information detailing personal data handling, legal processing bases, retention, and your statutory rights under UK GDPR."
  complianceBadge="UK GDPR & Data Protection Act 2018"
  activeSlug="privacy-policy"
  lastUpdated="February 2026"
>
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      1. Introduction &amp; Data Controller
    </h2>
    <p>
      {siteSettings.legalName} ("Techsteps", "we", "our", or "us") is dedicated to protecting and upholding the privacy, confidentiality, and security of all personal data entrusted to us. This Privacy Policy details our operational and technical procedures regarding the collection, use, transfer, and retention of personal data collected through our website, client portals, quote requests, and formal contractual engagements across our four divisions: Information Management, IT Lifecycle Services &amp; Destruction, Secure Shredding &amp; Document Integrity, and Moving &amp; Relocation Services.
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1 font-mono">
      <div><strong>Data Controller:</strong> {siteSettings.legalName}</div>
      <div><strong>Company Registration:</strong> {siteSettings.registrationNumber}</div>
      <div><strong>Registered Address:</strong> {siteSettings.address.street}, {siteSettings.address.city}, {siteSettings.address.county}, {siteSettings.address.postcode}, UK</div>
      <div><strong>Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) Tier:</strong> Data Controller Registered</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      2. Categories of Information We Collect
    </h2>
    <p>
      Depending on how you interact with Techsteps, we collect and process several categories of information:
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">A. Business Contact &amp; Account Data</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Full name, corporate email address, business telephone number, organizational title, company name, registered business number, and VAT registration identifiers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">B. Operational Logistics &amp; Site Access Information</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Collection and delivery site addresses, building security contact details, site access permits, vehicle height/loading constraints, and visitor clearance data required for our BS 7858 security-screened operatives.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">C. Asset Tracking &amp; Chain-of-Custody Documentation</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Hardware serial numbers, asset tag IDs, barcode records, Waste Transfer Notes (WTNs), Hazardous Waste Consignment Notes, and joint sign-off digital signatures.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-2xs">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">D. Technical &amp; Diagnostic Browsing Data</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          IP addresses, browser type, operating system, page performance metrics, and consent logs collected via privacy-preserving telemetry without cross-site tracking.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      3. Lawful Bases for Processing Under UK GDPR
    </h2>
    <p>
      In compliance with Article 6 of the UK GDPR, we only process personal information where a valid lawful basis applies:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600">
      <li>
        <strong>Contractual Performance (Article 6(1)(b)):</strong> Necessary to generate commercial quotations, verify logistics feasibility, dispatch vetted transport vehicles, execute data destruction agreements, and issue formal Certificates of Destruction.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal &amp; Regulatory Compliance (Article 6(1)(c)):</strong> Mandatory retention of statutory duty-of-care documentation under the Environmental Protection Act 1990, Hazardous Waste Regulations 2005, and HMRC tax record keeping mandates.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate Business Interests (Article 6(1)(f)):</strong> Maintaining network resilience, fraud prevention, security audit logging, and responding to business-to-business corporate enquiries.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Explicit Consent (Article 6(1)(a)):</strong> For non-essential cookies and targeted corporate insight updates where you have positively opted in.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      4. Data Security &amp; Protective Safeguards
    </h2>
    <p>
      We deploy multi-layered organizational and technical controls aligned with our ISO 27001 and Cyber Essentials Plus accreditations:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Personnel Vetting</div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">100% of staff undergo mandatory BS 7858 security screening and criminal record checks prior to handling client records.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Transport Telematics</div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">Live GPS tracking, geo-fenced routes, and deadlocked solid-sided vehicles for all physical media transfers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Cryptographic Controls</div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">All digital systems utilize AES-256 encryption at rest and TLS 1.3 encryption in transit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Physical Facility Security</div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">24/7 RedCare-monitored CCTV, biometric access airlocks, and dual-custody vault protocols.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      5. Data Retention Schedules
    </h2>
    <p>
      We retain personal data strictly for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was gathered and to satisfy UK statutory obligations:
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 font-bold">
            <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Record Category</th>
            <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Statutory / Business Basis</th>
            <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Retention Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 text-slate-600">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-medium text-slate-800">Standard Waste Transfer Notes (WTN)</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Environment Agency Duty of Care Regs</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-mono">2 years minimum</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-medium text-slate-800">Hazardous Waste Consignment Notes</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Hazardous Waste (England &amp; Wales) Regs</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-mono">3 years minimum</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-medium text-slate-800">Certificates of Destruction &amp; Erasure</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Contractual warranty &amp; ADISA audit standard</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-mono">7 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-medium text-slate-800">Commercial Invoices &amp; Fiscal Ledgers</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200">HMRC Statutory Requirements</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-mono">6 years + current FY</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-medium text-slate-800">General Web Enquiries (Uncontracted)</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200">Legitimate interest follow-up</td>
            <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 font-mono">12 months after last contact</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      6. Your Statutory Rights Under UK GDPR
    </h2>
    <p>
      As an individual whose personal data is processed by Techsteps, you hold enforceable rights under UK data protection law:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
      <li><strong>Right to Access (SAR):</strong> Request confirmation and an unredacted copy of all personal data held about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate, misleading, or incomplete records.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Erasure ("Right to be Forgotten"):</strong> Request deletion of your personal records where no overriding legal requirement to retain them exists.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Restriction:</strong> Request limitation of processing while an accuracy or legitimate interest dispute is assessed.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Object:</strong> Object to processing carried out under the basis of legitimate interests or direct business-to-business marketing.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> Receive electronic records provided to us in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="pt-2">
      We respond to all verified statutory rights requests within one calendar month without charging a fee, as mandated by the UK GDPR.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      7. Contacting the Data Protection Officer &amp; Escalations
    </h2>
    <p>
      To exercise your data protection rights, report an inquiry, or raise questions regarding our handling of your information, please contact our appointed Data Protection Officer:
    </p>
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono">
      <div><strong>Attention:</strong> Data Protection Officer (DPO)</div>
      <div><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:dpo@techsteps.co.uk" class="text-emerald-700 hover:underline">dpo@techsteps.co.uk</a> / <a href="mailto:compliance@techsteps.co.uk" class="text-emerald-700 hover:underline">compliance@techsteps.co.uk</a></div>
      <div><strong>Postal:</strong> {siteSettings.legalName}, {siteSettings.address.street}, {siteSettings.address.city}, {siteSettings.address.county}, {siteSettings.address.postcode}</div>
      <div><strong>Telephone:</strong> {siteSettings.phone}</div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 pt-2">
      If you remain dissatisfied with our response, you maintain the right to lodge a formal complaint with the UK supervisory authority: Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-700 underline">ico.org.uk</a>).
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPageLayout>
